66 [(5)] (e) establish informal working groups consisting of public and private stakeholders as is
appropriate to assist the center in fulfilling the requirements of this section; and
68 [(6)] (f) report to the commission as requested regarding the center's progress in fulfilling the
requirements of this section.
70 (2) The attorney general, on behalf of the state, shall provide for the registration and protection of a
trademark used by an organization described in Subsection (1)(c).
