187 Section 3. Section 63G-16-301 is amended to read:
188 63G-16-301. Definitions.
As used in this part:
148 (1) "Applicable federal agency" means the federal agency that issued a federal guidance letter.
150 (2) "Commission" means the Federalism Commission created in Section 63C-4a-302.
151 (3) "Education entity" means:
152 (a) the State Board of Education;
153 (b) the Utah Board of Higher Education;
154 (c) the State Charter School Board created in Section 53G-5-201;
155 (d) a local school board described in Title 53G, Chapter 4, School Districts; or
156 (e) a charter school governing board described in Title 53G, Chapter 5, Charter Schools.
157 [(2)] (4) "Federal agency" means a department, agency, authority, commission, council, board, office,
bureau, or other administrative unit of the executive branch of the United States government.
160 [(3)] (5)
(a) "Federal guidance letter" means a written statement by a federal agency, regardless of format, that:
162 (i) clarifies or provides instruction on:
163 (A) the federal agency's interpretation of a federal law; or
164 (B) the federal agency's policies for administering a federal law; and
165 (ii) is nonbinding and of general applicability.
166 (b) "Federal guidance letter" does not include:
167 (i) a written communication between a federal agency and a state agency regarding a specific entity;
169 (ii) a peer-to-peer communication; or
170 (iii) a written communication between a federal agency and the State Tax Commission containing
guidance related to the protection, storage, or safeguarding of confidential information.
173 [(4)] (6) "Federal law" means:
174 (a) a statute passed by the United States Congress; or
175 (b) a rule or regulation adopted by a federal agency.
176 [(5)] (7) "State agency" means:
177
